            <ArticleTitle>[Anaphylactic accidents due to glaphenine. 5 cases].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2797-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors report 5 cases of shock type anaphylactic reactions after the ingestion of glafenine. Up to the present, acute tubulo-interstitial nephritis had chiefly been reported. The existence of allergy to this medication remains to be proved by the wider application of allergological studies.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
